<!-- std.collections.md -->
# `std.collections`

`std.collections` (11): the collections beyond the prelude's `list`,
`dict`, `set` and `Arena`, written in Sisu over `list`. The prelude's
collections are reached from here too (`from std.collections import
Arena`).

Each type's doc examples are tests: `sisu test --std` runs them.

## Re-exports

- `list`: `std.core.list`
- `dict`: `std.core.dict`
- `set`: `std.core.set`
- `Arena`: `std.core.Arena`
- `Key`: `std.core.Key`
- `Slice`: `std.core.Slice`
- `Iter`: `std.core.Iter`
- `Entry`: `std.core.Entry`

## Contents

- [`Deque`](#Deque): A double-ended queue: values go in and come out at either end.
- [`Heap`](#Heap): A priority queue: `pop` takes the smallest value first (a binary heap over a list, so `push` and `pop` take time logarithmic in its size).
- [`SortedDict`](#SortedDict): A map whose keys are kept in order (11 names a B-tree; stage 0's is a sorted list, searched by halves): `keys` and `items` go from the smallest key up, whatever order they were inserted in.
- [`SortedSet`](#SortedSet): A set whose values are kept in order (11's B-tree set; stage 0's is a sorted list, searched by halves): `values` goes from the smallest up.
- [`BitSet`](#BitSet): A set of small non-negative integers, one bit each, in 64-bit words.

<a id="Deque"></a>
## `Deque`

```sisu
pub struct Deque[T]
    front: list[T]
    back: list[T]

impl[T] Len for Deque[T]
impl[T: Eq] Contains[T] for Deque[T]
```

A double-ended queue: values go in and come out at either end.

Two lists hold it, the front one reversed, so each end is a list's end;
taking from an empty end moves the other list across, so a value is
moved a constant number of times on average.

```sisu
var q: Deque[int] = Deque.new()
q.push_back(2)
q.push_back(3)
q.push_front(1)
assert len(q) == 3
assert q.pop_front() == Some(1)
assert q.pop_back() == Some(3)
assert q.pop_front() == Some(2)
assert q.pop_front() == None
```

<a id="Deque.new"></a>
### `Deque.new`

```sisu
pub pure def new() -> Deque[T]
```

An empty queue.

<a id="Deque.push_back"></a>
### `Deque.push_back`

```sisu
pub pure def push_back(mut self, own x: T)
```

Adds `x` after the last value.

<a id="Deque.push_front"></a>
### `Deque.push_front`

```sisu
pub pure def push_front(mut self, own x: T)
```

Adds `x` before the first value.

<a id="Deque.pop_front"></a>
